A turn on spare time runs on while a thread with time waits for the core,
so a thread that has time waits for the tick behind one that runs on what nobody wanted.

Caught-by: fuzz fuzz-pmp8 fuzz-rp2350 fuzz-smp2 fuzz-work qemu-replay
Report: a turn on spare time runs while a thread with time waits
Witness: fuzz spare-turn-ends-at-wake

diff --git a/kernel/sched.c b/kernel/sched.c
--- a/kernel/sched.c
+++ b/kernel/sched.c
@@ -1069,7 +1069,6 @@ void sched_tick(uint32_t ticks)
 static void spare_end(struct core *core)
 {
     if (core->run_queue != 0 && !core->recall && sched_spare_turn(core)) {
-        sched_turn_end();
     }
 }
 
